{"name":"Golden Chalice","hex":"#e7c068","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"chalice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large drinking cup, often having a stem and base and used especially for formal occasions and religious ceremonies.","A kind of water-cooled pipe for smoking cannabis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chalice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chalice","blocks":[{"text":"A chalice is a drinking cup raised on a stem with a foot or base. Although it is a technical archaeological term, in modern parlance the word is now used almost exclusively for the cups used in Christian liturgy as part of a service of the Eucharist, such as a Catholic mass. These are normally made of metal, but neither the shape nor the material is a requirement. Most have no handles, and in recent centuries the cup at the top has usually been a simple flared shape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/German_-_Chalice_with_Saints_and_Scenes_from_the_Life_of_Christ_-_Walters_44116.jpg/330px-German_-_Chalice_with_Saints_and_Scenes_from_the_Life_of_Christ_-_Walters_44116.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalice","wikidata":"Q210723"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"htt